# Protection from red stops red creatures blocking the enchanted creature (CR 702.16f) though Red Ward's Aura stays.
# Bot2's Devoted Hero wears Red Ward and attacks on turn 4: Bot1's red Mons's Goblin Raiders may not block it (the
# refusal), while the black Cabal Evangel may (the positive control), so Bot1 takes no damage.

[Bot1 Deck]
Swamp
Mox Ruby
Mox Jet
Cabal Evangel
Mons's Goblin Raiders
Swamp x12

[Bot2 Deck]
Plains
Mox Pearl
Devoted Hero
Red Ward
Plains x12

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Swamp.Play
Bot1.Hand.Mox Ruby.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Jet.Cast
Bot1.Battlefield.Swamp.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Jet.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Cabal Evangel.Cast
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Ruby.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Mons's Goblin Raiders.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
[T2 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Plains.Play
Bot2.Hand.Mox Pearl.Cast
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Battlefield.Plains.Activate
Bot2.Hand.Devoted Hero.Cast
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Battlefield.Mox Pearl.Activate
Bot2.Hand.Red Ward.Cast(Bot2.Battlefield.Devoted Hero)
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Pass
[T4 Bot2.Main1]
? Bot2.Battlefield.Red Ward.AttachedTo = Devoted Hero
? Bot2.Battlefield.Devoted Hero.ProtectionFrom = Red
Bot2.Attack(Devoted Hero > Bot1)
! Bot1.Block(Mons's Goblin Raiders > Devoted Hero)
Bot1.Block(Cabal Evangel > Devoted Hero)
[T4 Bot2.Main2]
[Expect]
Bot1.Battlefield.Cabal Evangel.Damage = 1
Bot2.Graveyard = Red Ward; Devoted Hero
Bot1.Life = 20
